  {
    "id": "cook.argv.dash#1",
    "name": "cook.argv.dash",
    "row": 51,
    "file": "module_utils/connectome_cook.py",
    "line": 37,
    "start": 1250,
    "end": 1273,
    "before": "not arg.startswith('-')",
    "after": "True",
    "why": "Line 37 is one compound condition shared with cook.argv.flag-position. Replacing only the dash sub-expression removes the refusal of option-like values: an argument starting with '-' is accepted at any index, with or without recorded flag positions. text() and credential_shaped() stay in force.",
    "source_sha256": "9fe0b847b07e46d7ea8e1591d50a54e845f9574e5bb2aa37e392c9f1e4c8c2c3"
  },
  {
    "id": "cook.argv.flag-position#1",
    "name": "cook.argv.flag-position",
    "row": 51,
    "file": "module_utils/connectome_cook.py",
    "line": 37,
    "start": 1258,
    "end": 1298,
    "before": "startswith('-') or index in flag_indices",
    "after": "startswith('-') or arg in [argv[i] for i in flag_indices]",
    "why": "Same compound condition at line 37; only the sub-expression 'index in flag_indices' changes. The exemption stays, but it is granted by value instead of by recorded index, which removes exactly the positional rule ('a value equal to a flag is not exempt'). A plain True here would be semantically the same mutant as cook.argv.dash (the whole parenthesis becomes True), so the two names could not be told apart; this replacement still refuses option-like values that equal no recorded flag.",
    "source_sha256": "9fe0b847b07e46d7ea8e1591d50a54e845f9574e5bb2aa37e392c9f1e4c8c2c3"
  },
  {
    "id": "cook.argv.validate-first#1",
    "name": "cook.argv.validate-first",
    "row": 51,
    "file": "module_utils/connectome_cook.py",
    "line": 317,
    "start": 17938,
    "end": 17976,
    "before": "validate_arguments(argv, flag_indices)",
    "after": "pass",
    "why": "Occurrence 1 is the call at line 317 (occurrence 0 is inside command(), line 43). Removes the validation of the whole assembled cook argv before any subprocess. The same argv is still validated inside command(), but only after verify_cook has already spawned its Git children, so only the validate-before-first-subprocess ordering is removed.",
    "source_sha256": "9fe0b847b07e46d7ea8e1591d50a54e845f9574e5bb2aa37e392c9f1e4c8c2c3"
  },
